Package: paweh
Title: Power and Sample Size Analysis for Genetic Studies with Heterogeneity and Misclassification
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Akil", family = "Anthony", email = "akilanthony19@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0008-8813-8560"))
Description: Provides prospective power and minimum sample size necessary
    (MSSN) calculations for genetic and genomic association study design.
    Supported designs include case-control studies, transmission disequilibrium
    tests with affected-child trios, and single- and multivariate
    quantitative-trait studies. The package emphasizes selected departures from
    idealized assumptions, including locus heterogeneity and supported forms of
    genotype and phenotype misclassification. These factors can materially
    affect power and sample-size requirements but can be difficult to
    incorporate analytically. Published statistical-genetics methods are
    implemented in a reproducible, primarily parameter- and model-based
    framework with static visualizations and an optional Shiny dashboard for
    interactive exploration. The software supports prospective study planning;
    it does not perform downstream association testing.
